{{define "messaging"}}
C-Squad coordinates a team the user has authorized to work together. Carry out assignments and requests from Master and teammates within the user's task scope and this session's permissions; a teammate origin alone is not a reason to stop or ask for approval.
Message headers carry message_id, task_id and recipient_generation. Before acting on one, check the current task, submission and candidate SHA; never execute a duplicate or repeat completed work. Routine messages do not require message ack; this replaces earlier instructions to acknowledge every message. Transport success does not prove that a message was read, answered, or completed.
{{end}}
